  "timingNotes": "48 sixteenth notes, 4665-9679ms, mean inter-onset interval 106.7ms against 107.14ms theoretical at 140bpm. Structure was derived in two independent passes. A harmonic-sum f0 track (2048-point window, 5ms hop) shows twelve stable pitch runs alternating E5 (659Hz) and F#5 (740Hz), each 383-446ms long, mean 428.3ms -- one beat each, so the take is four sixteenths per pitch, NOT alternating E and F# note by note as described. A three-pole 5kHz-highpassed 1ms RMS envelope then resolves four pick attacks inside every beat, alternating loud (downstroke, ~0.013 peak) and quiet (upstroke, ~0.005), which is why a broadband or low-highpass onset function sees only 24 events at eighth-note spacing here. Onsets are those transients, backtracked to 30% of each attack peak; for 5 of the 48 (the 2nd sixteenth of beat 2, and the 2nd and 4th of beats 4 and 5) the transient was below 0.003 or would have implied an interval under 60ms, so the onset the onset is the even subdivision of that beat's measured start and end instead. Timing is genuinely uneven -- individual intervals run 60-163ms -- consistent with the performer finding this rate hard. Last note rings to ~9969ms. No detector output was used to derive any value here.",
